  "question": {
    "text": "The spin-only magnetic moment value of the ion among \\(\\mathrm{Ti}^{2+}, \\mathrm{V}^{2+}, \\mathrm{Co}^{3+}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{Cr}^{2+}\\), that acts as strong oxidising agent in aqueous solution is _______ BM (Near integer).\n(Given atomic numbers : \\(\\mathrm{Ti}: 22, \\mathrm{~V}: 23, \\mathrm{Cr}: 24, \\mathrm{Co}: 27\\))",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Strong oxidising agent $=\\mathrm{Co}^{+3}$\nNo. of unpaired $\\mathrm{e}^{-}$in $\\mathrm{Co}^{+3}\\left[3 \\mathrm{~d}^6\\right]=4$\nHence $\\mu=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{n}+2)}=\\sqrt{24} \\mathrm{BM}$\nNearest integer $=5$",
    "image": null
  },
